A Mobile Robot is equipped with 2 independant rangefinders pointing at the same target.

Sensor A reports a distance of 2.0m with a variance of 0.04.
Sensor B reports a distance of 2.1m with a variance of 0.01.

Without Calculating the exact final position, which sensor's reading should the robot's state estimator trust more heavily and why does its variance curve dictate that decision

Sensor B is more accurate since its variance is lower and the lower the variance, the more precise the sensor; Its variance curve dictates this since its curve is more narrow and higher, meaning the robot has a smalelr range to assume its position out of.
